<title>UKRAINE: Ukraine industrial production fell 5.1 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Ukraine industrial production fell 5.1 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Industrial production in Ukraine fell 5.1 percent last year after a decline of 12.7 percent in 1995, the statistics ministry said on Tuesday.</p>
<p> UKRAINE INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION  DEC 96  NOV 96   DEC 95</p>
<p> mth/mth change (percent)	 -3.3    -1.3     -4.7</p>
<p> year/year change (percent)     -5.1    -5.0     -12.7</p>
<p>With the exception of October and March, Ukrainian industrial output declined every month in 1996.</p>
<p>The government has forecast industrial growth of 1.7 percent in 1997.</p>
<p>--Yuri Kulikov, Kiev newsroom, +380 44 229 2264</p>
